// The `prelude.files` sub-module: read a `file`'s content and metadata, and produce / release blobs.
// A `file` value carries only a reference into the project's blob store — the bytes and the metadata
// stay runtime-side — so these primitives are the bridge for the moments either must be read, or a
// value-plane base64 blob must become a real `file`.

@"The `file` a handle names is gone — it was `free`d, or the id never named a blob in this project (a
model hallucinating a `$katari_ref`). One error covers both: a slim handle cannot tell which. Thrown by
every reader below."
data gone(message: string)

@"The @content@ passed to `from_base64` is not valid base64 (bad alphabet, length, or padding)."
data malformed_base64(message: string)

@"The file's bytes, base64-encoded — the inline shape multimodal model APIs take. The whole content
materialises as one string. Throws `gone` if the handle no longer names a live blob."
primitive agent read_base64(value: file) -> string with prelude.throw[gone]

@"The file's recorded MIME type (e.g. \"image/png\"), read from the project's file catalog; \"\" when
none was recorded. Throws `gone` if the handle no longer names a live blob."
primitive agent content_type(value: file) -> string with prelude.throw[gone]

@"The file's size in bytes, read from the project's file catalog (no content download). Throws `gone`
if the handle no longer names a live blob."
primitive agent size(value: file) -> integer with prelude.throw[gone]

@"Make a `file` from a base64 string, lifting embedded bytes off the value plane and into a real blob
handle. The new file is owned by the current run and reclaimed with it (or explicitly, via `free`); two
calls with the same bytes are two different files. Throws `malformed_base64` if @content@ is not valid
base64."
primitive agent from_base64(@"The file's bytes, base64-encoded." content: string, @"The MIME type to record (e.g. \"image/png\"); \"\" to record none." content_type: string) -> file with prelude.throw[malformed_base64]

@"Release a file the current run owns, freeing its bytes now rather than at run teardown. Idempotent
and silent: freeing an already-gone file, or one the run does not own (a user-uploaded file), is a
no-op, so a retried block that frees the same handle twice behaves identically each attempt. A later
read of a freed handle throws `gone`."
primitive agent free(value: file) -> null
